+## Proposed security incident collector — Stage B, security review pending
+
+This is the unpublished proposal for [#2138](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/issues/2138), building on merged [Stage A PR #2203](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/pull/2203). Stage B is offline-qualified code, not deployed or accepted production operation. Code review: [Stage B PR #2204](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/pull/2204). Source hashes and qualification results are retained in [Stage B evidence](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/blob/feat/security-collector-stage-b/ops/security-collector/stage-b-evidence.json); resource/security requirements and rollback contract accompany it under `ops/security-collector/`. Publication of this section needs security/architecture approval; production ingestion needs separate approval.
+
+Pinned node-agent v0.3.310 source supports native HTTP single/bulk `RuntimeAlerts`, configurable headers/projected bearer tokens and bounded retry queues. Those queues are process memory, not restart-durable delivery. Stage B instead pulls the existing stderr JSON through verified HTTPS Kubernetes log reads, requiring no node-agent configuration change. It verifies a allowlisted named agent Pod UID and DaemonSet UID, ServiceAccount, metal6 node, exact pinned image or previously qualified amd64 child, running container/restart count and independent enrolled Deployment/ReplicaSet/Pod/image attribution. No listener, receiver, agent reconfiguration, RBAC binding or production scheduler ships.
+
+The reader retains only normalized observations, hashed log anchors, replay receipts and coverage state in one private SQLite database. Queue and cursor commit together; replay is idempotent across restart. Defaults cap pending records at 1,000 / 8 MiB, SQLite pages at 64 MiB, incidents at 200, seven-day receipts at 20,000 and accepted observations at 1,000/hour. Provision a separate rollback-journal/filesystem budget; proposed resources are unmeasured and require rollout qualification. Saturation stops acceptance without evicting pending evidence or live receipts. Raw process arguments, environment, packages/paths and payloads stay out of state/public projection.
+
+Kubelet logs remain lossy. Initial boundaries, missing overlap anchors, restart/replacement, disconnection, malformed/oversized snapshots, backpressure and absent checks are explicit gaps. Gap state latches; reconnect/replay does not certify missing intervals. A quiet successful poll is a reader heartbeat, not proof of detector liveness or complete emission. Polling has a persisted 15-second minimum interval, and health checks expire after five minutes. A future private external supervisor must detect stopped processes/unwritable status; no new monitoring stack is proposed.
+
+The assessment reader never submits scans, acquires the runner lock, clears fences or modifies active CronJobs. It joins retained execution/request/terminal/checksum records and latest attempt/coverage with a repository-verified Grype identity, then independently rereads named report/SBOM/summary objects and current controller/Pod UID, generation, readiness and running digest. All replicas must agree. Before/after history, objects and inventory must be stable. Overall failed latest batches conservatively gate even cached peer successes. Missing, failed, stale, excluded, unsupported and incomplete coverage cannot erase last-qualified vulnerabilities or authorize recovery.
+
+Existing runner records contain UID/digest but no historical generation. Stage B therefore requires an independent observation of the current UID/generation/digest epoch before a scan starts. Current coverage cannot retroactively qualify older reports. An ordinary scheduled assessment after that observation can qualify; no extra scan or #2135 acceptance change is included. UID recreation, generation/digest changes, evidence expiry and source gaps invalidate recovery. Report age is at most 72 hours, DB age seven days, latest batch/coverage 26 hours and independent inventory one hour. Pending assessments recovered after a crash require fresh requalification matching the complete canonical validated observation before ingestion. Pending/receipt identity conflicts produce unknown telemetry and invalidate assessment-based resolution while preserving queued evidence, cursors and receipts. Older receipts without an observation hash remain preserved and cannot authorize vulnerability replay; neither a matching event ID nor a persisted clean flag is sufficient.
+
+Public issue writes and automatic closure remain disabled. The coordinator defaults disabled and only returns safe previews after explicit local enablement. Publication requires reviewed workload aliases and typed identifiers/digests/times/counts, fixed investigation text and configured same-repository references. Raw evidence and private Gitea findings never enter public issues. Gatus owns service-health issues, Kyverno owns policy issues, and neither can resolve a security incident. Production GitHub integration remains a separate gate.
+
+Proposed production permissions are read-only namespace Roles for enrolled Deployment/Pod/ReplicaSet inventory, one reviewed agent Pod log and named assessment resources. Use a dedicated short-lived API token and verified CA/origin; no Secrets, exec, scan submission, workload writes or GitHub credential is needed. Run one unprivileged writer with a read-only root filesystem, no host access, a private bounded state volume and continuously updated trusted history mounted read-only. Do not move scanner pods or modify active jobs to provide history access. Cilium `policyEnforcementMode=never` remains unchanged: NetworkPolicy is not isolation. Actual RBAC denied-access tests, egress controls, source identities, live history access, resources and supervision require separate qualification.
+
+Offline tests use synthetic pinned exporter/Grype envelopes and the active runner's actual history/coverage contracts, isolated files/SQLite, mocked external writes and a local HTTPS server. They demonstrate source → reader → validation → collector → durable state → safe preview, restart/replay, source gaps, malformed inputs, changed images/UIDs/generations, expired evidence and storage saturation. They do not demonstrate live collection, unattended runtime behavior or a production rollback.
+
+Rollback while undeployed is to keep the coordinator disabled and revert the code PR, preserving private state. For a separately approved installation, disable its scheduler/readers through reviewed Flux and revoke only its read credential if needed. Preserve SQLite/pending queue/cursors/receipts/gaps/inventory epochs, unresolved write fences and existing issues; record the stop as missing telemetry. Stop the writer before copying state and any recovery journal. Restore with writes disabled, check integrity/size, replay runtime safely and independently requalify queued assessments. Do not clear gaps/fences, discard pending evidence, delete scanner reports/SBOMs/history/PVCs, close issues in bulk or weaken policies. Actual rollout/reconnect/rollback and this Wiki proposal need review before enablement.
